  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India. Household financial flows and stocks, new capital issues, mutual funds, gold and silver prices, market capitalisation, turnover and derivatives, and the company finance studies are read from India Atlas's archived copy of the RBI's DBIE database. The Survey of Professional Forecasters is read from the RBI Innovation Hub's copy of DBIE. Listed-company tables use archived official DBIE CAS observations and prompted statistical reports; eight historical industry-margin cells retain an explicitly flagged ambiguous mirror selection. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">{guideRevisionSummary}</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked against the RBI's own publications: household flows in the Bulletin (October to December 2025), the public limited company study of 2024-25 (release of 30 March 2026), the listed-company CAS/report overlap and all thirty annual and quarterly prompted exports through April to June 2026, the 101st round of the forecasters' survey, the Handbook's gold table, and the Bulletin's new issues table.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Rupee amounts are converted to ₹ crore and shown in ₹ lakh crore. Shares of household saving are computed from the RBI's rupee figures. Every DBIE report repeats each value once per display unit; one is kept. Company study growth rates and ratios are taken from each year's own study; rupee levels are kept study by study and never joined. Nothing is estimated or interpolated.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Household flows are preliminary and revised. Breaks kept apart: the company studies' change to the Ind AS format (from the 2020-21 study); the forecasters' move to the new GDP and CPI bases (from round 99); the capital issues table's calendar years before 1981-82 and its two layouts.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0 (October 2026). Stock index levels (Sensex, Nifty and others) are left out: they are the exchanges' licensed products. Foreign portfolio flows are in the external account guide; interest rates on commercial paper and deposits in the interest rates guide.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>India Atlas, savings, markets and companies</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2">{guideRevisionSummary}</span></span>
      <span>Set in Source Serif 4 and Golos Text</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

